# Milestone 4 Lesson Overviews

## Lesson 8: Defending Your Data

#### Lesson 8 is a **Develop & Critique** lesson. Students synthesize their safety investigations and draft clear, evidence-based Safety & Privacy Guidelines for their Responsible AI Use Guide.

### 📝 **Lesson Overview**
<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block; width: 100%">
<a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/aid-thinking-critically-about-ai-2025/units/1/lessons/8" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
Access Lesson 8: Defending Your Data
</a>
</p>

<!-- Warm Up -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 12px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px; border-radius: 6px;">
<summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
Warm Up (5 minutes)
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.4;">
<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students recap their Lesson 7 explorations and identify patterns across shopping data, public profiles, and social media scenarios.
</p>
</div>
</details>

<!-- Activity -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 15px; border-radius: 6px;">
<summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
Activity (35 minutes)
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.4;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt"><b>🔄 Jigsaw Synthesis</b></p>

<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students meet in Expert Groups to solidify findings, then transition into Jigsaw Groups to identify cross-cutting risks and strategies.
</p>

<p style="font-size: 14pt"><b>🛡️ Project Work</b></p>

<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students draft the <strong>Safety & Privacy</strong> section of their Responsible AI Use Guide.
</p>

<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Each guideline must:
</p>

<ul style="font-size: 13pt; margin-top: 5px;">
<li>Be actionable and realistic</li>
<li>Reference specific evidence from explorations</li>
<li>Balance AI usefulness with human safety</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students focus on building a “Privacy Shield” that prioritizes human agency and critical skepticism.
</p>

</div>
</details>

<!-- Wrap Up -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 15px; border-radius: 6px;">
<summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
Wrap Up (5 minutes)
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.4;">
<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students add a new question to the Want to Know column of their KWL Chart and reflect on one strategy they will personally use moving forward.
</p>
</div>
</details>

### 🧾 **What to Prepare**:
* #### Ensure students bring their Milestone 4 Learning Log.
* #### Preview the Safety & Security project level.
* #### Prepare instructions for Expert and Jigsaw group transitions.
* #### Review expectations for evidence-based guidelines.

### 💡 **Tips for Teaching**:
* #### Push for nuanced recommendations rather than “never” or “always” rules.
* #### Require students to tie at least one guideline to a concrete exploration example.
* #### Encourage reflection on long-term digital habits, not just classroom scenarios.
MARKDOWN
